  "narrative": {
    "intro": "North Dakota has registered $600M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Award count is 1,959 with an average award size of $306K. Obligations fell 26.9% year over year. These are partial fiscal-year totals, so the current-year numbers do not represent a full 12-month period. Year-by-year history shows fluctuations: FY21 was $780M, FY22 was $973M, FY23 was $803M, FY24 was $980M, and FY25 was $821M. The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer in the state with $272M in obligations so far this fiscal year, followed by the Department of Defense with $144M and the Department of Transportation with $86.1M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the top vendor at $256M, and the Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers industry accounts for $219M of obligations. This snapshot highlights a smaller FY2026 to date total compared with several recent fiscal years and shows concentration in health-related buying and vendors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting trended in North Dakota recently?",
        "body": "Obligations are $600M in FY2026 to date, down 26.9% year over year. Recent fiscal years varied: FY21 was $780M, FY22 was $973M, FY23 was $803M, FY24 was $980M, and FY25 was $821M. The FY2026 to date total is lower than FY24 and FY22. Totals for the current fiscal year are partial and may change as the year progresses."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal spending in North Dakota?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services leads with $272M, followed by the Department of Defense at $144M and the Department of Transportation at $86.1M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the largest vendor at $256M, with WALSH FEDERAL LLC at $74.4M and PACKET DIGITAL LLC at $27M. The Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers industry accounts for $219M of obligations, indicating a strong health spending concentration."
      }
    ]
